[38;5;231m⏺[39m Added to [38;5;153mindex.html[39m: a labeled native checkbox inside [38;5;153m<main>[39m, plus one CSS rule that strikes through the label text
  when it's checked.

  Using [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m means the on/off state is handled by the browser — no JavaScript needed. Wrapping it in
  a [38;5;153m<label>[39m makes the text clickable and keeps it accessible.

  Two things it deliberately does not do, since you asked for basic: the state isn't persisted across reloads, and
  there's no way to add new items — the one row is hardcoded. Say the word if you want either.

